paperman (1.4.0-1VENDOR_VERSION) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Run on Windows 10 and 11 (x64 and Arm), with an installer and a TWAIN
    back end for scanners, and on macOS (Apple Silicon and Intel), with a
    disk image carrying its own SANE
  * Add a Linux AppImage and a snap, besides the .deb
  * Scanning: auto size and straightening by the scanner, auto colour,
    blank-page detection in colour, sideways feeding, a Long size for
    sheets longer than Legal, recovery from misfeeds and jams, Stop
    keeping the sheets already fed, and much faster transfer from
    Fujitsu scanners
  * Add the scan modes Mono, Dither, Grey, Colour and Auto, and presets
    which keep more of the scan panel and can be updated and renamed
  * Scan from the command line (--scan), with --log and --sane-debug for
    finding out what went wrong
  * Unfold scanned booklets into their pages
  * Browse, open, change and scan into repositories on a paperman server,
    with changes shown as they happen
  * Follow the desktop's dark theme, with dark icons
  * Offer somewhere to keep papers on a first run, and lay the window out
    to suit the screen
  * Add a fake Fujitsu scanner for testing without paper (Linux)

 -- Simon Glass <sjg@chromium.org>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:33:50 -0600

